<article class="env-lemma" id="00PG">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/00PG">Lemma <span data-tag="00PG">10.119.12</span> <span class="named">(Krull-Akizuki)</span>.</a>  Let $R$ be a domain with fraction field $K$. Let $L/K$ be a finite extension of fields. Assume $R$ is Noetherian and $\dim (R) = 1$. In this case any ring $A$ with $R \subset A \subset L$ is Noetherian. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $I \subset A$ be a nonzero ideal. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0H7L" data-tag="0H7L">10.30.8</a> we can find a nonzero element $x \in I \cap R$. Then we get $I/xA \subset A/xA$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/00PF" data-tag="00PF">10.119.11</a> the $R$-module $A/xA$ has finite length as an $R$-module. Hence $I/xA$ has finite length as an $R$-module. Hence $I$ is finitely generated as an ideal in $A$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>